---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "@/partials/PageHeader.astro";
---

<Base>
  <PageHeader title="Privacy Policy" />
  <section class="section pt-14">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="content">
        <h3>Privacy Policy for Horsemen of the Hopocalypse</h3>

        <strong>Effective Date: July 1, 2026</strong>

        <p>
          Horsemen of the Hopocalypse ("Horsemen of the Hopocalypse," "the
          Club," "the Site," "we," "us," or "our") respects the privacy of
          visitors to
          [https://horsemenofthehops.com/](https://horsemenofthehops.com/). This
          Privacy Policy explains what personal information is collected through
          the Site, how that information is used, and the choices available to
          users.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy is intended to help the Site provide a conspicuous
          online privacy notice that identifies the categories of personal
          information collected, whether information is shared, how policy
          changes are communicated, and the policy’s effective date, which are
          core elements commonly required for website privacy disclosures.
        </p>

        <strong>Information Collected</strong>
        <p>
          The Site may collect the following categories of personal information
          when voluntarily submitted through forms, email, or other direct
          contact:
          <ul>
            <li>Name</li>
            <li>Mailing address</li>
            <li>Telephone number</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
          </ul>
        </p>

        <p>
          The Site does not state that it uses cookies, analytics tools,
          tracking pixels, or similar automated technologies for visitor
          monitoring.
        </p>
        <p>
          CalOPPA separately requires websites used by California residents to
          disclose how they respond to Do Not Track signals and whether third
          parties may collect personally identifiable information across time
          and across websites.
        </p>

        <strong>How Information Is Used</strong>

        <p>
          Personal information collected through the Site may be used to:
          <ul>
            <li>Respond to inquiries and communications.</li>
            <li>
              Provide information about club activities, events, membership, or
              related matters.
            </li>
            <li>
              Maintain internal records related to communications and club
              administration.
            </li>
          </ul>
          Personal information is not sold.
          <br />
        </p>
        <br />

        <strong>Sharing of Information</strong>

        <p>
          The Site does not use third-party services for processing personal
          information and does not sell personal information. Personal
          information is therefore intended to be used internally for the Club’s
          own communications and administration, except where disclosure is
          required by law or reasonably necessary to protect legal rights. The
          categories of third parties with whom personal information may be
          shared are therefore limited to:
          <ul>
            <li>
              Service providers or hosting providers only to the extent
              technically necessary to operate the website.
            </li>
            <li>
              Government authorities, law enforcement, or other parties when
              disclosure is required by law. the extent technically necessary to
              operate the website.
            </li><li>
              Government authorities, law enforcement, or other parties when
              disclosure is required by law.
            </li>
          </ul> CalOPPA requires a privacy policy to describe the categories of third
          parties with whom personally identifiable information may be shared, if
          any.
          <br />
          <br />
        </p>

        <strong>Review and Updates</strong>

        <p>
          Individuals who have submitted personal information may request to
          review, update, or correct that information by contacting the Club
          using the contact information below. CalOPPA identifies disclosure of
          any review-and-correction process as one of the items a compliant
          privacy policy should include.
        </p>

        <strong>Do Not Track</strong>

        <p>
          Because the Site does not state that it uses analytics, advertising
          technology, or cross-site tracking tools, the Site does not currently
          respond differently to browser Do Not Track signals. The Site also
          does not state that third parties collect personally identifiable
          information about users’ online activities over time and across
          different websites through the Site.
        </p>

        <strong>Children’s Privacy</strong>

        <p>
          The Site is not intended for children under 13, and personal
          information should not knowingly be collected from children under 13.
          The federal COPPA rule imposes specific obligations on operators of
          websites or online services directed to children under 13 or that
          knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.[2] If
          the Club becomes aware that personal information has been submitted by
          a child under 13 without appropriate consent, that information should
          be deleted as appropriate.
        </p>

        <strong>Data Security and Retention</strong>

        <p>
          The Site should use reasonable administrative and technical measures
          to protect personal information from unauthorized access, use, or
          disclosure. Personal information should be retained only for as long
          as reasonably necessary to respond to inquiries, administer club
          activities, comply with legal obligations, or resolve disputes.
          Texas’s data privacy law generally requires covered businesses to
          provide an accessible privacy notice with disclosures about the
          categories of personal data processed, purposes of processing,
          consumer rights, categories of personal data shared with third
          parties, and categories of third parties receiving the data.[3]
        </p>

        <strong>Changes to This Policy</strong>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Any material
          changes should be reflected by updating the effective date at the top
          of this page and posting the revised Privacy Policy on the Site.
          CalOPPA specifically requires disclosure of the process used to notify
          users of material changes to the policy.[1]
        </p>

        <strong>Contact</strong>

        <p>
          Questions or requests relating to this Privacy Policy may be directed
          to:
          <ul>
            <li>Horsemen of the Hopocalypse</li>
            <li>
              Website: <a href="https://horsemenofthehops.com/"
                >horsemenofthehops.com</a
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              Email: <a href="mailto:horsemenofthehopocalypse@gmail.com"
                >horsemenofthehopocalypse@gmail.com</a
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
